Upstream components

The translation checkpoint contains language-model parameters initialized from
Uni-Sign's mT5 model. mT5 (multilingual Text-to-Text Transfer Transformer, the
reader's language backbone) was developed by Google Research.

mT5: https://github.com/google-research/multilingual-t5
Uni-Sign initialization: https://huggingface.co/ZechengLi19/Uni-Sign

The reconstruction checkpoint uses a DINOv3 pretrained visual backbone.
DINOv3: https://github.com/facebookresearch/dinov3

Body-parameter decoding and surface simulation use external Momentum Human Rig
assets. Momentum Human Rig: https://github.com/facebookresearch/MHR

These upstream components retain their respective licenses and notices.

Sentence encoders used for translation scoring

SBERT (Sentence-BERT): shibing624/text2vec-base-chinese, revision
183bb99aa7af74355fb58d16edf8c13ae7c5433e.

SimCSE: cyclone/simcse-chinese-roberta-wwm-ext, revision
871d7039a3fccd4869d545a25b63c545341ca7f4.

These two encoders are supplied with the evaluation asset bundle that accompanies the
code package, reproduced from those repositories at the revisions above, and they keep
their own licences.
